WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.852 --> 00:00:07.132
In this video, you'll see how many students at your school have practiced each graduate attribute this year.

2
00:00:07.633 --> 00:00:21.403
Select Graduate Evidence in the menu. The page always shows the current school year. It counts students whose teachers hold a seat on your license, and shows counts and percentages only. No student or teacher is named.

3
00:00:21.904 --> 00:00:36.764
Under By group, each row is a classroom, with its number of students and how many attributes those students have practiced. Classrooms are numbered, not named. Small classrooms are combined into one row so no one can be picked out.

4
00:00:37.264 --> 00:00:50.154
Below that, each attribute shows how many students have practiced it. Dark means they finished an activity connected to it, and light means a related activity. It shows practice, not how well a student did.

5
00:00:50.656 --> 00:00:56.446
If no activity is connected to an attribute yet, the page says so instead of showing zero.

6
00:00:56.947 --> 00:01:04.187
To share this with your principal or board, select Print this report. The menu and buttons stay off the printed page.

7
00:01:04.688 --> 00:01:12.838
These connections are Fixer Nation's own mapping to New York's frameworks. Neither New York State nor CASEL has endorsed them.
